            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0477" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/10–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-01T16:00:00-04:00">November 1, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>653. Urtels 787, Oct. 27 and 795, October 30. You are authorized to give the
                    Soviet and British Ambassadors a copy of your note to the <pb facs="0478"
                        n="466" xml:id="pg466"/> Prime Minister. While concurrence of the Iranian
                    Government is not strictly necessary, you will doubtless wish to clear with
                    Saed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
